WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.216
Start with the system task, rather than asking which name sounds most powerful.

2
00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:11.488
Embedded control needs a dedicated program and platform interfaces,

3
00:00:11.488 --> 00:00:13.219
memory and interrupts.

4
00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:16.682
GPIO, UART and SPI are platform peripherals,

5
00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:20.931
not features automatically contained in the CVA6 core.

6
00:00:20.931 --> 00:00:27.776
PMP is a physical-memory protection mechanism; its settings are held in dedicated CSRs.

7
00:00:27.776 --> 00:00:32.340
CSR is a broader category of control and status registers,

8
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.117
not a second independent memory-protection unit.

9
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:40.287
Here, a Linux host means a conventional paged system,

10
00:00:40.287 --> 00:00:45.796
requiring suitable privilege modes, MMU translation and boot software.

11
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:48.707
Cheshire is a named platform example.

12
00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:54.451
Accelerator management needs coordinating software and system interfaces.

13
00:00:54.451 --> 00:00:59.172
CV-X-IF extends instruction execution through a coprocessor;

14
00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:04.287
mentioning it does not establish that Occamy uses this interface.

15
00:01:04.287 --> 00:01:10.346
Occamy illustrates a CVA6 manager working with a separate Snitch accelerator.

16
00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:14.359
The SDK and FPGA flow are development entry points,

17
00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:19.788
not proof that every illustrated control application has been tested.

18
00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:24.195
For FPGA prototypes or ASIC integrations, configuration,

19
00:01:24.195 --> 00:01:27.342
platform and software must fit together.

20
00:01:27.342 --> 00:01:29.860
Next, compare actual parameters.

